  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya bilateral programme - resilience, peace and stability</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective of the Programme is to promote resilience, peace and stability in Kenya by curbing violent extremism, preventing man-made and natural crises, and strengthening Kenya&apos;s pro-active role in regional peace and security and as a host-community for refugees. (SDG 1, SDG 6, SDG 10, SDG 16, SDG 17).

The Programme will be implemented by NGO Act Change Transform (ACT!), Kenya who will be working on resilience, peace and stability; Water Sector Trust Fund (WSTF) who will be working on Access to Water and sanitation in the Arid and Semi- Arid Lands (ASALs) in Kenya; Northern Rangelands Trust (NRT) who will be working on community resilience and adaptation to climate change through sustainable investments in nature based solutions (NbS), water and renewable energy in Northern and Coastal Kenya; and Danida Fellowship centre (DFC) who will build the capacity of NRT on Nature based solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
